{"id":"71baef3e-43fc-4e74-9e4a-debac843313b","expr":"result != null && (result.isEmpty() || !result.contains(\".\"))","rationale":"Result is empty string if clazz is null or has no package; otherwise, it is package path with '.' replaced by PATH_SEPARATOR, so no '.' remain.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#classPackageAsResourcePath(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.566075780Z"}
{"id":"3967ef0f-8ead-473e-9b6b-48f1023ddae3","expr":"clazz == null || result.equals(\"\") || result.equals(clazz.getPackage().getName().replace('.', '/'))","rationale":"The method returns '' for null or no package; else it returns the package name as resource path, thus for non-null clazz with package, result equals the package name replacing '.' with '/'","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#classPackageAsResourcePath(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.566075780Z"}
{"id":"8f478ecd-2f05-4340-906e-de6b2fd32ccc","expr":"clazz == null || (result.startsWith(clazz.getPackage().getName().substring(0,1).replace('.', '/')) || result.equals(\"\") )","rationale":"If clazz has package, result reflects that package path, so it must start with first segment; if clazz is null, result is empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#classPackageAsResourcePath(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.566075780Z"}
{"id":"0b7e01f2-6f4e-49a3-8947-a3eaf99c1e50","expr":"instance != null","rationale":"The parameter 'instance' must not be null at method entry due to the explicit assertion in the method body.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesAsSet(Object):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.612918444Z"}
{"id":"3b7243c1-78e3-40dd-ac12-5da82997681e","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Since the method returns getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet for a valid class, the result should never be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesAsSet(Object):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.632728929Z"}
{"id":"6042a34a-5a5d-44e3-b5a0-9567c0f5ba7e","expr":"!result.contains(null)","rationale":"Since the set represents interfaces, it should not contain null elements.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesAsSet(Object):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.632728929Z"}
{"id":"6d6b701d-6d18-45c1-834f-1ed1dcde285f","expr":"instance.getClass().isInterface() || !result.contains(instance.getClass())","rationale":"The returned set is all interfaces implemented; the concrete class of instance is not included unless it is itself an interface.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesAsSet(Object):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.632728929Z"}
{"id":"e80cf1fe-e571-485e-b7e0-b1699230db01","expr":"collection == null || !collection.isEmpty() || collection.isEmpty()","rationale":"to check that collection is either null or empty or non-empty (covers all cases, but relevant because method calls depend on emptiness state)","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#toClassArray(Collection<Class<?>>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.941285714Z"}
{"id":"2e0892e5-8038-438f-9cd0-ec1a4ba66e75","expr":"collection == null || collection.toArray().getClass().isArray()","rationale":"Ensures that the result of collection.toArray is an array","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#toClassArray(Collection<Class<?>>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:57.941285714Z"}
{"id":"27ded143-93dd-4664-be61-7b7d64eab6a9","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method returns an array, never null, as it returns either the input collection converted to an array or a constant empty array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#toClassArray(Collection<Class<?>>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.745869788Z"}
{"id":"90eb3b31-c63d-4411-abc0-4f2e880dbb5b","expr":"(!collection.isEmpty() || result.length == 0)","rationale":"If the collection is empty or null, the returned array is the EMPTY_CLASS_ARRAY, which is empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#toClassArray(Collection<Class<?>>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.745869788Z"}
{"id":"3ac816b3-e44b-4492-94b4-9941fdc30e7b","expr":"collection == null || result.length == collection.size()","rationale":"When the collection is non-empty, result array length equals the collection's size due to toArray call.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#toClassArray(Collection<Class<?>>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.745869788Z"}
{"id":"2a585a28-9eca-411d-a500-351bfa60df4a","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The klass parameter must be non-null for the method to retrieve interfaces.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.796479759Z"}
{"id":"eafd94b9-8a62-4fd9-8a59-66b92598d570","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive()","rationale":"Since the method intends to retrieve interfaces, the class should not be a primitive type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.796479759Z"}
{"id":"a22b75e7-b46b-4622-af6a-767df0bfa647","expr":"!clazz.isArray()","rationale":"Typically, arrays are not considered when searching for interfaces implemented, so likely not an array type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.796479759Z"}
{"id":"574c6ec6-b882-4c4a-a7a5-a66281b38896","expr":"clazz.getSuperclass() != clazz","rationale":"Ensures the superclass is not the same class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:14:58.796479759Z"}
{"id":"2c1488d7-8ebf-40c6-a7d8-86eb32005269","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method processes the input class to determine interfaces; it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.117807466Z"}
{"id":"40dcefda-1317-45b1-9626-4bb57802699e","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive()","rationale":"Primitive types do not have interfaces, so the class passed is likely not primitive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.117807466Z"}
{"id":"0df08ee1-a3a1-4bb4-8ae4-b3b204b9a8d3","expr":"clazz.isInterface() || clazz.getSuperclass() != null","rationale":"The class either is an interface or has a superclass, relevant to interface retrieval.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.117807466Z"}
{"id":"ea3ab372-be20-4074-8ccd-7bf97dad5029","expr":"!clazz.isArray()","rationale":"Array types behave differently and may not have interfaces in the conventional sense.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.117807466Z"}
{"id":"8b03c377-b82f-4482-b0a2-e4bdb7f45216","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method asserts that clazz must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.387858486Z"}
{"id":"d3bf18a3-7268-4a5b-8788-3623554a9459","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive()","rationale":"Primitive types do not implement interfaces, so typically the input is expected not to be primitive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.387858486Z"}
{"id":"16528ec4-68fb-483d-b9eb-c59cb7f534cb","expr":"!clazz.isArray()","rationale":"Arrays are handled differently, so the typical usage expects non-array clazz.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>,ClassLoader):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.387858486Z"}
{"id":"461a6b61-0b9e-4839-a1eb-1e85b54b1d1e","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method getAllInterfacesForClass returns an array; usually it returns a non-null array containing all interfaces implemented by the class or an empty array if none.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.454347925Z"}
{"id":"9190ad7a-e428-4114-a6e9-865f00b58599","expr":"result.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length is always greater or equal to zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClass(Class<?>):Class<?>[]","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.454347925Z"}
{"id":"0937d937-b999-44ae-9b21-df97391aec56","expr":"clazz1 == null || clazz2 == null || clazz1 != clazz2","rationale":"Both classes can be null or different; no guarantee of equality at method entry.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.456662522Z"}
{"id":"a88687fc-e9de-4b78-9079-b23ba9367962","expr":"clazz1 == null || clazz2 == null || clazz1.isAssignableFrom(clazz2) || clazz2.isAssignableFrom(clazz1) || clazz1.getSuperclass() != null","rationale":"If both classes are non-null, either one is assignable from the other or clazz1 has a superclass.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.456662522Z"}
{"id":"115b59f2-917a-4d46-8949-6f09d258fa4b","expr":"clazz1 == null || clazz2 == null || (!clazz1.isAssignableFrom(clazz2) && !clazz2.isAssignableFrom(clazz1)) || clazz1.getSuperclass() != null","rationale":"If neither class is assignable from the other, clazz1 must have a superclass to find a common ancestor.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.456662522Z"}
{"id":"6267c411-b7ef-4d5d-9c94-bcbd87cb4558","expr":"result == null || (result.isAssignableFrom(clazz1) && result.isAssignableFrom(clazz2))","rationale":"The method returns a class that is the common ancestor of clazz1 and clazz2, so the result must be assignable from both.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.506422360Z"}
{"id":"3ae0e325-fe87-4d72-9aba-577d8aaaaa6a","expr":"(clazz1 == null && result == clazz2) || (clazz2 == null && result == clazz1) || (clazz1 != null && clazz2 != null)","rationale":"By the contract, if one input is null, the result is the other input; if both are non-null, result is computed.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.506422360Z"}
{"id":"5d50ea4f-14e1-446d-8bc7-878d3b7db75e","expr":"result == null || (result != clazz1 || !clazz2.isAssignableFrom(clazz1))","rationale":"The method returns clazz1 if clazz1 is assignable from clazz2, so if result equals clazz1, this must hold.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.506422360Z"}
{"id":"f07ccd5c-acfe-4d5d-aeeb-51a17f1e7197","expr":"result == null || (result != clazz2 || !clazz1.isAssignableFrom(clazz2))","rationale":"Similarly, the method returns clazz2 if clazz2 is assignable from clazz1, so if result equals clazz2, this must hold.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.506422360Z"}
{"id":"32d68360-f692-4370-ae93-02c0164e4624","expr":"result != null || (clazz1 != null && clazz2 != null && !clazz1.isAssignableFrom(clazz2) && !clazz2.isAssignableFrom(clazz1))","rationale":"The method returns null only when both classes exist and no class is assignable from the other or common ancestor (except Object).","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.506422360Z"}
{"id":"e12816c9-4fdc-4389-984b-ac4d1d89190c","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method likely expects a non-null class to process.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.948384579Z"}
{"id":"19ede22d-0583-49f3-a634-ed293c175d7b","expr":"clazz.isInterface() || clazz.getInterfaces().length >= 0","rationale":"The array returned by getInterfaces is non-null, thus the length is at least 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.948384579Z"}
{"id":"9f740da2-4495-4184-b9b2-306196fd07e0","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive()","rationale":"Primitive types cannot implement interfaces.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.948384579Z"}
{"id":"a1a38840-fd9a-4814-bbe2-9ccaf611d11f","expr":"(clazz.isArray() || clazz.isPrimitive()) || clazz.getSuperclass() != null","rationale":"Almost all classes except Object have a superclass; arrays and primitives are special cases.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.948384579Z"}
{"id":"decf1bbd-1ae1-42a1-a3e2-6dec18796995","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive() || clazz.getTypeName() != null","rationale":"The class's type name string is always available.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:00.948384579Z"}
{"id":"a4c7d01f-28df-4330-9ea2-8a18f40547c0","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The result set of interfaces should always be non-null regardless of the class.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:01.646654109Z"}
{"id":"97a46db6-3786-4eea-89f3-fbd27251f896","expr":"!result.contains(null)","rationale":"The returned set of interfaces should not contain any null elements.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:01.646654109Z"}
{"id":"a412bf82-0618-457b-abe1-ef96ae3f91d7","expr":"clazz.isInterface() ? result.contains(clazz) : true","rationale":"If the input class is an interface, it is included among the returned interfaces.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getAllInterfacesForClassAsSet(Class<?>):Set<Class<?>>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:01.646654109Z"}
{"id":"e60c1df4-61cd-47db-a43e-5c9aaf63c078","expr":"interfaces != null","rationale":"The array 'interfaces' is asserted to be non-empty, hence it is not null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#createCompositeInterface(Class<?>[],ClassLoader):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.268282706Z"}
{"id":"f801909a-e6de-4b9d-992c-ec59f30941fe","expr":"interfaces.length > 0","rationale":"According to Assert.notEmpty(interfaces), the array length must be at least 1.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#createCompositeInterface(Class<?>[],ClassLoader):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.268282706Z"}
{"id":"d848de31-b958-44e8-b4b7-dc5653ebd5c4","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The parameter clazz must be non-null to safely call clazz.isMemberClass().","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.337257154Z"}
{"id":"169ac4ea-ee69-4370-841e-a15413e3b285","expr":"clazz.isMemberClass() == (clazz.getEnclosingClass() != null)","rationale":"A class is a member class if it has a non-null enclosing class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.337257154Z"}
{"id":"6ab89dba-e8ae-4a22-b7e5-7a4583142d93","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive()","rationale":"Primitive types do not have member classes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.337257154Z"}
{"id":"2bd009ac-31a2-40e1-bbb5-d34da83f096d","expr":"!clazz.isArray()","rationale":"Array types cannot be member classes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.337257154Z"}
{"id":"db285627-3825-4884-9493-17b3863d3cd7","expr":"clazz.isMemberClass() || !clazz.isLocalClass()","rationale":"Classes that are member classes are generally not local classes, providing a useful state predicate.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.337257154Z"}
{"id":"f2f3af81-0af0-45ab-be58-798924988c8c","expr":"!result || clazz.isMemberClass()","rationale":"If the class is an inner class, it must be a member class.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.385909111Z"}
{"id":"742c5674-ad64-47eb-b997-cf79dca8ecd4","expr":"result == (clazz.isMemberClass() && !clazz.isStatic())","rationale":"Assuming isStaticClass delegates to clazz.isStatic(), the returned value matches that expression.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.385909111Z"}
{"id":"94e52f0c-4310-4f93-bb8f-d8e9e2058f17","expr":"result == false || clazz.isMemberClass()","rationale":"If it is considered an inner class, it must satisfy being a member class.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isInnerClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.385909111Z"}
{"id":"26d716be-3c68-47c5-a407-8d6f453d939e","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"null check for safe method calls","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isLambdaClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.428531002Z"}
{"id":"23cae154-a3f4-4b50-b77a-1ba9f958080f","expr":"clazz.isSynthetic() == false || clazz.getInterfaces().length > 0","rationale":"If synthetic, must implement interfaces","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isLambdaClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.428531002Z"}
{"id":"5090c6bf-d9d4-4625-8842-f4ba504fc928","expr":"clazz.getInterfaces().length >= 0","rationale":"Interfaces length is non-negative","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isLambdaClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.428531002Z"}
{"id":"5317fc5b-9343-4849-8deb-abac9024570e","expr":"!result || clazz.isSynthetic()","rationale":"The method's condition requires clazz.isSynthetic() to be true for result == true.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isLambdaClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.468945118Z"}
{"id":"8b86fdf6-6f57-4e84-bb31-b74f9e8cd3a5","expr":"!result || clazz.getInterfaces().length > 0","rationale":"The method checks that the interfaces array length is positive when result is true.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isLambdaClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.468945118Z"}
{"id":"b9b61b71-1380-439a-9f56-8b1e5ebcf2e6","expr":"object != null","rationale":"The method calls object.getClass(), so object must be non-null to avoid NullPointerException.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxy(Object):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:15:03.507661911Z"}
