{"id":"c8cbe36d-6cf1-4214-a857-00bc3a150579","expr":"descriptor != null && !descriptor.isEmpty()","rationale":"Field descriptor is a JVM descriptor string; it must be non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:11.860846998Z"}
{"id":"d11e38aa-63b8-4fdb-b0b0-ed05181910c7","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"Method instructions require non-null owner, name, and descriptor strings to refer to a method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:13.845698903Z"}
{"id":"981ab928-b675-48ab-98f1-5fec85ba41ed","expr":"owner.length() > 0 && name.length() > 0 && descriptor.length() > 0","rationale":"Method references must have valid non-empty strings for owner, name, and descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:13.845698903Z"}
{"id":"cfd06974-c232-4329-9193-d05fb9af4c18","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The owner is the internal name of the method's owner class and is expected not to be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.862133168Z"}
{"id":"af9c2a41-99df-403e-a5a3-46e15de9a26a","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"The method name should be non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.862133168Z"}
{"id":"d6343acd-3af0-4928-98bc-e369c0f092d6","expr":"descriptor != null && descriptor.startsWith(\"(\") && descriptor.contains(\")\")","rationale":"The descriptor follows the JVM method descriptor format, starting with '(' and containing ')'.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.862133168Z"}
{"id":"56f54bca-c15e-44ec-a00c-5a54d186246b","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"Passing null for owner, name, or descriptor to add a fieldref is invalid; thus these values should be non-null at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.923177845Z"}
{"id":"117f76b8-eb38-4bab-9490-9b116429d146","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"A field must have a non-empty name to be valid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.923177845Z"}
{"id":"0eb98be5-da2e-4512-9718-58874139ac7b","expr":"owner.indexOf('/') >= 0","rationale":"The internal name of classes in JVM bytecode uses slashes as package separators.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:14.923177845Z"}
{"id":"bd554338-f833-4593-bfe0-fcf81622534f","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The method name of an invokedynamic instruction is typically required and not null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:16.514727916Z"}
{"id":"441a88bd-7619-4e36-9e7d-d5883a64aa8e","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method descriptor string must not be null for valid bytecode instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:16.514727916Z"}
{"id":"9c19a025-3515-42d6-90e3-ca78aed0a7b1","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"The bootstrap method handle parameter is required for invokedynamic and must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:16.514727916Z"}
{"id":"293e4e37-6cf9-423d-81e8-f8673105fd27","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"The name of the invokedynamic method is generally a non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:16.514727916Z"}
{"id":"6880ac23-a3db-4598-9474-289f579182e9","expr":"name != null","rationale":"Name of the method invocation should always be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:18.561736146Z"}
{"id":"654bfa6d-96ae-4ec1-80d7-b56e9147d387","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Descriptor string should always be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:18.561736146Z"}
{"id":"6d3d2870-3b29-49eb-9f12-df5bf59320fe","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"Bootstrap method handle must be non-null for invokedynamic.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:18.561736146Z"}
{"id":"9aef28a5-72fc-4dbc-a98d-c8256bd4a1fd","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"Bootstrap method arguments should either be null or an Object array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:18.561736146Z"}
{"id":"1a6cbbf4-8834-44f1-bcf7-15ef98b88e68","expr":"label != null","rationale":"visitLabel expects a non-null Label instance.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:21.139522019Z"}
{"id":"a2a2da46-c43f-4154-8aeb-35605ad9419c","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Labels represent positions in bytecode, so bytecodeOffset should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:21.139522019Z"}
{"id":"40e068b4-148d-42ba-9114-bf2f67c7f560","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter is used and must not be null to represent the jump target.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:21.286380020Z"}
{"id":"901be58b-51a3-4e34-82bb-937e49186651","expr":"(opcode >= 0) && (opcode <= 255)","rationale":"Opcode represents a single byte opcode value.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:21.286380020Z"}
{"id":"165e0f0a-254d-40ca-8a7c-8f65ec078999","expr":"label != null","rationale":"Since the method operates on label heavily, it must be non-null at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:23.845668820Z"}
{"id":"f6e05c0a-515d-4abc-9489-b6e8e62462d7","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Labels represent positions in bytecode and so their offsets should be non-negative at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:23.845668820Z"}
{"id":"302b8c8b-b6db-4587-bd6b-b84c9ee0da30","expr":"value != null","rationale":"Because visitLdcInsn is invoked with a value representing a constant to be loaded, this value is commonly non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:29.797366393Z"}
{"id":"32b22c5f-ded1-4ae3-8a94-a0d163144544","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"The varIndex parameter represents a local variable index, which cannot be negative in JVM bytecode.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:31.565262737Z"}
{"id":"bca17cb2-2e68-443d-9f97-530ec66d1a72","expr":"increment >= -128 && increment <= 127","rationale":"The increment is typically in the byte range -128 to 127 because it is stored as a byte in the non-wide IINC instruction.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:31.565262737Z"}
{"id":"4a12e8d5-de41-4457-8640-29b3cec03b29","expr":"(varIndex <= 255) || (increment > 127 || increment < -128)","rationale":"From the code, if varIndex is greater than 255 or increment is outside the signed byte range, the wide instruction is used.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:31.565262737Z"}
{"id":"f3e42c19-b500-42b7-b9c5-51c91a9c3e4d","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"In the wide instruction, varIndex is stored as two bytes, so it must be ≤ 65535.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:31.565262737Z"}
{"id":"a04fc03d-9959-40d5-8f7c-779a1e6d1108","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, local variable indices (varIndex) are expected to be non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:32.176672187Z"}
{"id":"94482ba5-f8ec-40d9-9c4d-8ac8f9e090fe","expr":"increment <= 127 || increment >= -128","rationale":"Method logic uses a WIDE instruction if increment > 127 or increment < -128, so increment usually fits in a byte range or requires a WIDE instruction.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:32.176672187Z"}
{"id":"c611df19-1722-4db4-a953-e3bbd4ed1b4c","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"varIndex is passed to putShort when WIDE instruction is used, indicating it's within short range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:32.176672187Z"}
{"id":"da098fc1-bac4-44bf-90f4-b60d3e959b53","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"Incrementing by zero might be unusual as it has no effect, but is not prohibited.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:32.176672187Z"}
{"id":"7ef7e053-a966-4a26-8ab2-57676efea024","expr":"varIndex < Integer.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"Given varIndex is an int, it should always be less than Integer.MAX_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:32.176672187Z"}
{"id":"5a185fd8-118a-44d3-9eb7-c8f9decf51b0","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels parameter represents the array of labels for each switch case, it must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.050559218Z"}
{"id":"30fe3170-c2bf-480b-96ba-ac0c1b713452","expr":"labels.length == (max - min + 1)","rationale":"A TableSwitch instruction expects a label for each value in the range [min, max].","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.050559218Z"}
{"id":"70711eaf-d41d-4fc6-97be-8cbb06ffb552","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"A valid range for the table switch requires min to be less than or equal to max.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.050559218Z"}
{"id":"f1c2b4d6-aef0-4b16-995d-87819a6d3b25","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default target label must be not null to handle unexpected keys.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.050559218Z"}
{"id":"f8732fc3-e01f-4d27-ae19-f9453dc1cd9a","expr":"labels[0] != null","rationale":"Since labels represent handler blocks, each must be a valid label reference, including the first one.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.050559218Z"}
{"id":"df808ef9-4850-49c9-a969-6ab63df322b9","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Default label must not be null as it represents the default handler block.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.098108540Z"}
{"id":"1e162a95-c920-4544-a03b-b205a0d587c0","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"Keys array must be non-null since it represents switch keys.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.098108540Z"}
{"id":"2b72c859-5d74-44d0-ae1b-213a1aa008c1","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"Labels array must be non-null as it is the array of handler blocks for keys.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.098108540Z"}
{"id":"0e49c7ca-48d7-49e3-982f-66943b460bec","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"Keys and labels arrays must have the same length to map each key to its label.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:36.098108540Z"}
{"id":"4a61c848-a535-40d5-a358-c5e835054101","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels argument must be a valid array of Label for the switch branches.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:37.275297118Z"}
{"id":"bd9175b9-dbbb-4683-9c3f-0e8d98692a2b","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"In a table switch instruction, the minimum key must be less than or equal to maximum key.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:37.275297118Z"}
{"id":"d1605311-fe60-4931-98a5-38f14a124594","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"The number of labels on the switch instruction matches the range size between min and max inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:37.275297118Z"}
{"id":"d906c203-681f-4ae9-af37-885bab7da25f","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Table switch instruction requires a non-null default label for unmatched cases.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:37.275297118Z"}
{"id":"b8dacebd-f1f2-4d6d-8f13-20459ced3911","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The keys array and labels array must be non-null to iterate and access elements safely.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:40.836302401Z"}
{"id":"27681a33-ff6f-4608-802a-0e8c24be8334","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"Each key value corresponds to a label. Their arrays must have equal length for the instruction to be valid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:40.836302401Z"}
{"id":"1b3b0aef-eeff-45ea-87d7-4cbd13cd249a","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label for the switch instruction must be a valid non-null label.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:40.836302401Z"}
{"id":"5e4825f6-3b83-4617-83d1-e39f17226b05","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"The keys array length must be non-negative since length is array length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:40.836302401Z"}
{"id":"12399b20-9996-4593-98c8-e41fe5ed0f68","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The 'labels' array should not be null since the method iterates over it.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:41.839921464Z"}
{"id":"18c82b4f-fafb-4b8e-a876-cc8d798537de","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label 'dflt' is used without null checks, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:41.839921464Z"}
{"id":"56e6bc71-2bda-4d0e-92eb-91907c069ae7","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:41.839921464Z"}
{"id":"9d9ab1f9-c7ca-4140-a840-a3a0dd5a0772","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label 'dflt' must not be null as it is used to add successors and mark flags.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:42.215218926Z"}
{"id":"1070c016-8aff-4ce1-8041-c80d458932ed","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array is used in the loop to add successors and mark flags, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:42.215218926Z"}
{"id":"44b1d608-5e6f-40d5-a123-ff6a33abd674","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"The labels array length must be non-negative as a basic array property and affects loop iteration.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:42.215218926Z"}
{"id":"460319be-8154-4cb3-90f0-d34001c6c4d2","expr":"dflt.getCanonicalInstance() != null","rationale":"To safely access 'flags' on the canonical instance of dflt, it must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:42.215218926Z"}
{"id":"27d146ed-c451-4f85-9c31-b59c3d6475bb","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor is a string representing the type, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:45.944611295Z"}
{"id":"6028cac8-67a9-4994-9bba-fd9def63f4d5","expr":"numDimensions > 0","rationale":"An array must have at least one dimension.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:45.944611295Z"}
{"id":"005923eb-3c9d-4846-b359-c759beb67b34","expr":"numDimensions <= descriptor.length()","rationale":"The descriptor encodes array type and dimensions, so its length should be at least numDimensions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:45.944611295Z"}
{"id":"38e369b4-8c24-4bc6-8700-d49a19dc5083","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"[\")","rationale":"The descriptor should start with '[' characters for array types.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:45.944611295Z"}
{"id":"c74c5ae3-fb45-4f51-968f-707e3a6338f2","expr":"numDimensions <= 255","rationale":"The JVM bytecode MULTIANEWARRAY instruction uses numDimensions as a byte.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:32:45.944611295Z"}
