{"id":"406c3bc7-e4cf-4a98-8efb-f9e96f2c7a79","expr":"permittedSubclass.length() > 0","rationale":"Permitted subclass internal names are expected to be non-empty strings.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:46.720951029Z"}
{"id":"3fcb5fbc-f3cd-4408-baea-a293d29e14dc","expr":"permittedSubclass.indexOf('/') >= 0","rationale":"Internal names in ASM use '/' characters to separate package components.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:46.720951029Z"}
{"id":"8c7ae40b-d4b2-4383-98dd-2694986cf883","expr":"permittedSubclass.equals(permittedSubclass.trim())","rationale":"It is customary for internal names not to contain leading or trailing whitespace.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:46.720951029Z"}
{"id":"5cf01d27-232e-41d2-9bfb-f2f4ae1cd51c","expr":"attribute == null || attribute.getClass().getName() != null","rationale":"The attribute object's class name should be non-null if attribute is non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitAttribute(Attribute):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:47.840298485Z"}
{"id":"34669c71-7be9-4c1c-b536-87bd0827984b","expr":"attribute == null || attribute.equals(attribute)","rationale":"For any non-null reference, the equals method must be reflexive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitAttribute(Attribute):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:47.840298485Z"}
{"id":"e2bdc3bd-b154-413f-bb35-1c444856588a","expr":"permittedSubclass == null || permittedSubclass.length() > 0","rationale":"If permittedSubclass is non-null, it should be a valid internal name string and thus have positive length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:49.733143868Z"}
{"id":"c225be37-5a76-404c-80b7-6d0b5c2f3794","expr":"permittedSubclass == null || !permittedSubclass.contains(\" \")","rationale":"Permitted subclass names, if non-null, do not contain spaces as they represent internal JVM names.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:49.733143868Z"}
{"id":"05fc3fc3-ab45-4e4c-a1a0-e81c0c4b7bcd","expr":"permittedSubclass == null || permittedSubclass.indexOf('/') >= 0","rationale":"If permittedSubclass is non-null, it should have the internal form containing '/' as package separators.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:49.733143868Z"}
{"id":"897bdc3b-f031-429e-a65f-85f3d15e0015","expr":"permittedSubclass == null || !permittedSubclass.isEmpty()","rationale":"The permittedSubclass string, if not null, should not be empty, as per its semantic as internal names.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitPermittedSubclass(String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:49.733143868Z"}
{"id":"7202f5d5-5148-4fea-a55f-9cc5736b85fb","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The internal name of the class must be non-null as it identifies the inner class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.314934288Z"}
{"id":"8d6759f6-9c47-4e9a-b51a-c1d0a4e71e46","expr":"(innerName == null) || (innerName.length() > 0)","rationale":"The innerName is either null (anonymous inner classes) or a non-empty simple name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.314934288Z"}
{"id":"8a58848b-5c4b-4d2a-bfb6-aaca105913be","expr":"(outerName == null) || (outerName.length() > 0)","rationale":"If the class is a member of another class or interface, outerName is non-null and non-empty; otherwise null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.314934288Z"}
{"id":"18e4ddf5-b213-404c-9614-0556d85bdeea","expr":"(access & ~0xFFFF) == 0","rationale":"Access flags combine standard JVM access modifiers which are within defined bitmask limits.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.314934288Z"}
{"id":"5e3655d7-4614-457b-a322-f19b7a7eebf3","expr":"access >= 0","rationale":"Access flags are unsigned flags represented in a signed int, but usually non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.314934288Z"}
{"id":"1b75f8ff-fdee-4def-a9cf-667fca15262d","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty() && descriptor != null && !descriptor.isEmpty() && (signature == null || !signature.isEmpty())","rationale":"Name and descriptor are essential strings for a record component and should not be empty or null. Signature can be null or a valid string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.859178535Z"}
{"id":"19f85575-7fa2-4d7f-8950-6df99fb86374","expr":"signature == null || signature.startsWith(\"<\")","rationale":"When signature is not null, it often represents a generic signature starting with '<'.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.859178535Z"}
{"id":"0745860e-2eb6-4bfb-868a-3d07a2f41e42","expr":"name.length() <= 255","rationale":"Name length is usually limited by JVM constraints, often less than 256 characters.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.859178535Z"}
{"id":"883e243c-dc82-42e4-8ccb-28726b7d80b5","expr":"descriptor.contains(\"/\") == false","rationale":"Descriptors of classes often contain '/' for package separators, so false indicates primitive or array types without '/'.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:50.859178535Z"}
{"id":"bfed9d7c-af54-48c6-b955-e82416885efc","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The 'name' parameter represents the internal name of an inner class and must be non-null as per JVM specifications.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.738917466Z"}
{"id":"eee0108a-ab71-41f1-8681-5193a2f4a76d","expr":"(outerName == null) || (outerName != null)","rationale":"The 'outerName' is null if C is not a member of a class or interface, which is allowed for local or anonymous classes.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.738917466Z"}
{"id":"b2b4cfce-f326-4859-a15f-a3f4d033f6bb","expr":"(innerName == null) || (innerName.length() > 0)","rationale":"The 'innerName' is the simple name of the inner class and should be null only for anonymous inner classes.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.738917466Z"}
{"id":"946f22bf-f64d-46c5-8da3-d2c72e89332d","expr":"(access & 0xFFFF) == access","rationale":"The 'access' parameter contains bit flags indicating access rights and modifiers within a valid range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.738917466Z"}
{"id":"205ffb63-2a07-4598-bbd8-bedcec1f7647","expr":"!((innerName == null) && (outerName != null))","rationale":"If an inner class has an outer name, it generally should also have an inner name since anonymous classes have null outerName.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitInnerClass(String,String,String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.738917466Z"}
{"id":"5351cfb4-1c9f-4cb8-baa1-ece6d8265517","expr":"!(result == null && (name == null || descriptor == null))","rationale":"If the result is null, then at least one of name or descriptor must be null; or conversely, if both are non-null, result should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.794510422Z"}
{"id":"e322d9d6-a883-4684-9111-8e4de3bcb138","expr":"result == null || (signature == null || signature.length() >= 0)","rationale":"If result is not null and signature is not null, signature is a string possibly empty, thus length >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitRecordComponent(String,String,String):RecordComponentVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:51.794510422Z"}
{"id":"fd3df630-2677-48af-a398-87b284209fdb","expr":"name != null","rationale":"Field names are expected to be non-null because they refer to the identifier of the field.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitField(int,String,String,String,Object):FieldVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.008112764Z"}
{"id":"1edcb1a1-f2d5-41fb-9152-81b2e8cffa2f","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Descriptor strings describe the type of the field and are required for correct bytecode processing.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitField(int,String,String,String,Object):FieldVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.008112764Z"}
{"id":"5e7b3999-46a3-4d8b-9a1a-4c1496e141ca","expr":"(access & 0x1) == 0 || (access & 0x1) == 1","rationale":"Access flags are bitmasks where specific bits represent modifiers; thus the expression verifies bits can be set or cleared.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitField(int,String,String,String,Object):FieldVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.008112764Z"}
{"id":"911ef713-28a4-44d4-9822-53fe748421dd","expr":"value == null || value != null","rationale":"Value is optional and can hold a constant value or be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassVisitor#visitField(int,String,String,String,Object):FieldVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.008112764Z"}
{"id":"0ba0bb7c-fe25-4317-8e29-d3df0dbb67af","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method performs calls on clazz, so it must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Class<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.755586249Z"}
{"id":"04dfb525-3014-49b2-80b2-6cb7ac77b081","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method is guaranteed to return a non-null Type instance.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Class<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.789962780Z"}
{"id":"242487d2-69f2-447b-a15d-be1df77b2fb6","expr":"constructor != null","rationale":"Method expects a non-null constructor parameter for processing.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.819999918Z"}
{"id":"894e15ce-de73-4e3e-a8cd-51da793bf4c9","expr":"!constructor.isSynthetic()","rationale":"The getType method likely expects a non-synthetic constructor to compute a descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.819999918Z"}
{"id":"65630fea-041e-4ecc-ba31-f51af528d9b0","expr":"constructor.getDeclaringClass() != null","rationale":"The declaring class is essential for the constructor descriptor and expected not to be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.819999918Z"}
{"id":"3d1dfd0d-dfba-4ace-ba28-4d811c98b009","expr":"constructor.getParameterCount() >= 0","rationale":"Parameter count of a constructor is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.819999918Z"}
{"id":"af274c09-75aa-4f07-9e23-1eeb98a1ffdd","expr":"constructor.getName() != null","rationale":"Constructor reflection API guarantees a non-null name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.819999918Z"}
{"id":"3b99795f-7d25-4244-8f3b-bb06d7d6feb2","expr":"constructor.getParameterCount() == 0 || result.getDescriptor().contains(\"(\")","rationale":"A constructor with parameters must have a descriptor containing parentheses.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.848234679Z"}
{"id":"2bf01988-94a9-4616-9421-4c90bcb3c230","expr":"!result.getInternalName().isEmpty()","rationale":"The returned Type represents a valid JVM type descriptor associated with the constructor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.848234679Z"}
{"id":"09ed7998-eda3-41dd-8094-51c30b6c093f","expr":"constructor.getDeclaringClass().getName().equals(result.getClassName())","rationale":"The returned Type corresponds to the class that declares the constructor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Constructor<?>):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.848234679Z"}
{"id":"31d518fa-9cb4-4402-964e-df6471a5c17f","expr":"method != null","rationale":"Since getType calls getMethodDescriptor(method), method must be non-null to avoid NullPointerException.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Method):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:33:53.874674487Z"}
