{"id":"499abd17-446e-4ffb-ac84-198cc4196014","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode parameter represents a bytecode instruction opcode, which should be a non-negative integer within a valid range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:17.918875670Z"}
{"id":"7e8cec97-f4f5-472a-8797-f47c4cf43a7d","expr":"opcode <= 202","rationale":"Opcodes for visited instructions in ASM lie between 0 and 202 inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:17.918875670Z"}
