{"id":"11bc79d5-0f28-4d71-a6bc-9251b8228c09","expr":"type.indexOf('/') >= 0","rationale":"Internal class names use '/' as separators instead of '.'","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:27.339338291Z"}
{"id":"1e6a6c4e-5fa8-48bb-ad09-3ecc08db6fad","expr":"type != null && !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The operand 'type' represents the internal name of a class and thus should not be null or empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:27.520150531Z"}
{"id":"4859e983-a009-4c9b-80a1-39df80480ba7","expr":"type.indexOf('/') >= 0","rationale":"Type internal names use slashes ('/') as separators instead of dots, so the presence of '/' indicates valid internal name format.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:27.520150531Z"}
{"id":"a105b39f-a477-41fc-a73f-39d6134d1b9d","expr":"owner != null && !owner.isEmpty()","rationale":"Owner represents the internal class name and should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.184869946Z"}
{"id":"dac1cf09-c835-4557-8f54-416f2d0a66c9","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"Name is the method name which must be valid and non-empty for method invocation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.184869946Z"}
{"id":"32a9f988-4cf8-4561-84c9-0f4752a690a5","expr":"descriptor != null && descriptor.startsWith(\"(\") && descriptor.contains(\")\")","rationale":"Descriptor is the method descriptor expected to start with '(' and contain ')' as per JVM specs.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.184869946Z"}
{"id":"8de87e82-32e0-4cbf-9d17-901f45f44d87","expr":"opcode == 178 || opcode == 179 || opcode == 180 || opcode == 181","rationale":"The opcode parameter for field instructions in JVM bytecode is restricted to these four values representing the four field instruction types.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.873306229Z"}
{"id":"96a7f527-6a49-49ba-913a-c59deab6fa91","expr":"owner != null && !owner.isEmpty()","rationale":"The owner string should be a valid internal class name for the field's owner, so it is usually non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.873306229Z"}
{"id":"a17348ee-28a7-4318-9c39-32501058bd62","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"Field names accessed by this method are expected to be valid Java identifiers and thus non-empty non-null strings.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:28.873306229Z"}
