{"id":"c210c64b-d66b-4f12-983b-f7986166ea9b","expr":"value != null || value == null","rationale":"Trivially true expression regarding nullness of value","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:39.097959212Z"}
{"id":"a17b9150-09b5-4e86-96ad-2354132685d4","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label for the jump instruction is expected to be a non-null target in bytecode manipulation.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:39.465407117Z"}
{"id":"5c249ac7-90d3-4bee-a10b-a7f9d460e05c","expr":"opcode >= 167 && opcode <= 201","rationale":"Jump instruction opcodes in JVM bytecode start from 167 (GOTO) to 201 (JSR_W); this bounds check covers valid jump opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:39.465407117Z"}
