{"id":"768b8dc2-60a9-41a6-af46-babaa8a4061a","expr":"(max - min + 1) >= 0","rationale":"The calculation of range (max - min + 1) is non-negative and valid.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:43.031819802Z"}
{"id":"336b45db-cd17-41b9-9b16-081147e25198","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"The method visitTableSwitchInsn is used to emit a TABLESWITCH bytecode instruction that covers keys from min to max inclusively, so max >= min must hold.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:44.508311912Z"}
{"id":"c2bd24ef-c400-4a19-b881-d0e4c602e612","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels parameter represents the handler blocks for each key and must be a non-null array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:44.508311912Z"}
{"id":"b4101fd4-4173-43f7-a419-508104e826fb","expr":"labels.length == (max - min + 1)","rationale":"The labels array size corresponds exactly to the number of keys covered by the TABLESWITCH instruction.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:44.508311912Z"}
{"id":"7562ace5-0332-4957-affc-86b4fe5b31ca","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The dflt parameter corresponds to the default handler label for keys outside the range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:44.508311912Z"}
{"id":"fe76a7f4-7983-4839-87b9-d42acfc0e655","expr":"labels.length > 0","rationale":"Since max >= min, the labels array must be strictly positive in length reflecting the switch cases.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:44.508311912Z"}
{"id":"b7290138-ef4a-4eb4-8fbd-cd2494be002c","expr":"value != null","rationale":"While null is a valid constant in JVM, often in ASM visitLdcInsn uses a non-null value. Here the invariant allows checking that value is not null if the method usage forbids it.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:45.255030975Z"}
{"id":"71e94638-87d2-4216-bbb9-d7157fa4dd5a","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label dflt must be a valid Label object indicating the default block","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.241309665Z"}
{"id":"1f0360d0-4299-4621-9b54-5c0f1b684184","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"keys array must be non-null to hold the switch keys","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.241309665Z"}
{"id":"3b78e0bc-6ca3-495c-8f69-9c105c81fa79","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"labels array must be non-null to hold the handler blocks per key","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.241309665Z"}
{"id":"3c1adb46-c61c-4272-92f0-59408f73ede1","expr":"(keys.length == labels.length)","rationale":"Each key has a corresponding label so keys.length equals labels.length","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.241309665Z"}
{"id":"bb91730c-7375-4ce0-8bac-2fe41d55bc0d","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"keys array is used to define keys in the lookup switch instruction and must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.901874203Z"}
{"id":"2c2999ef-4e08-4189-8b73-182445850bbb","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"labels array is used for target labels in the lookup switch instruction and must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.901874203Z"}
{"id":"be9c54a3-a08a-481d-b55c-d40d6c065305","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"The number of keys must be equal to the number of target labels to maintain correct mapping.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.901874203Z"}
{"id":"8a9ebe5d-9113-44bc-8280-2e5220e2cf91","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Default label for the switch cannot be null to define default handler block.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:46.901874203Z"}
{"id":"377ef1d2-7d70-41af-b530-d6625cde1f91","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor must be non-null to represent a valid array type descriptor for the MULTIANEWARRAY instruction.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:47.019738513Z"}
{"id":"15839f17-eabb-4fcf-bb3f-06bd7a3f283e","expr":"numDimensions > 0","rationale":"numDimensions must be positive since it represents the number of dimensions for a multi-dimensional array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:47.019738513Z"}
{"id":"13242804-2e62-4ffc-8747-bc7ebdbe76ff","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"[\")","rationale":"Array type descriptors in JVM bytecode start with '['; this checks that the descriptor is of an array type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:47.019738513Z"}
