{"id":"fd9624ca-63ae-416e-9298-18bbaa69916e","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The handler label indicates the start of exception handling code; it should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:50.802297008Z"}
{"id":"1298a76c-5705-48f3-8c19-de26854e3bf3","expr":"(type == null) || (type.length() > 0)","rationale":"The type string can be null for finally blocks or must be non-empty if specified.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:50.802297008Z"}
{"id":"03e3760f-dc3f-4a10-a788-a929f518bc34","expr":"start != end","rationale":"The try block must have a valid scope thus start and end labels cannot be the same.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:50.802297008Z"}
{"id":"165de9c0-801a-452e-ad80-e19ce857e24b","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The start label marks the beginning of the try block and cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:51.350031542Z"}
{"id":"af6d4ac8-4623-40c6-a624-35b2a14e3c4c","expr":"end != null","rationale":"The end label marks the end of the try block and cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:51.350031542Z"}
{"id":"56d8d0dd-a5c5-4bbe-8da7-b275c13ac073","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The handler label must be non-null to indicate where the exception handler starts.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:51.350031542Z"}
{"id":"6d855df2-5911-41cb-9de6-b26398e48930","expr":"type == null || !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"If type is not null, it must be a non-empty internal name string identifying the caught exception type.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:51.350031542Z"}
{"id":"fc3c23db-fd7f-4c8d-b6e4-b805a3eb2c11","expr":"start != end","rationale":"The start and end labels cannot be equal, since they mark the inclusive start and exclusive end of the try block.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:51.350031542Z"}
{"id":"eb326586-4f3f-4600-b98c-71e50afd40b3","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Descriptor string must be non-null to describe the annotation class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:52.824302783Z"}
{"id":"442c324f-5b01-479c-be58-3ddf9f98fc7c","expr":"visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"Visible flag is a boolean and can only be true or false.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:52.824302783Z"}
{"id":"0799e646-621d-4063-916f-95eb0f3d1dd8","expr":"typeRef >= 0","rationale":"typeRef is an int that is used as a reference and typically non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:52.824302783Z"}
{"id":"191d7adb-718a-4605-a159-4106cda50aa8","expr":"name != null","rationale":"Name should be a non-null String identifying the local variable.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:54.423904818Z"}
{"id":"d2383607-3aa6-4817-99c9-f836eb6b070e","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Descriptor should be a valid JVM type descriptor string, non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:54.423904818Z"}
{"id":"a0cf3552-f644-47db-97cf-659cfe1a1864","expr":"start != null","rationale":"Start label must be a valid instruction label marking the beginning of the variable's scope.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:54.423904818Z"}
{"id":"38353788-7303-4671-bf8f-c3d3c88c29fa","expr":"end != null","rationale":"End label must be a valid instruction label marking the end of the variable's scope.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:54.423904818Z"}
{"id":"5a9d83a1-7717-4358-9590-123643cdd438","expr":"index >= 0","rationale":"Local variable index must be non-negative since it refers to a position in the local variables array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:54.423904818Z"}
{"id":"f6403399-ee08-4a4f-9546-43df5f0da853","expr":"name != null","rationale":"A local variable must have a valid non-null name identifier for proper debugging and processing.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:56.014076745Z"}
{"id":"49ad39b2-843e-47b3-b838-e6679eece008","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor provides the type of the local variable and is necessary for correct classification.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:56.014076745Z"}
{"id":"472720b9-d0fc-4cde-a49c-0637400dc7f1","expr":"start != null && end != null","rationale":"A valid local variable scope must have a defined start and end label; both cannot be null as they specify the variable's lifetime.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:56.014076745Z"}
{"id":"7a645398-b9d9-4448-b12f-6cba5b7d95bf","expr":"index >= 0","rationale":"The index indicates the slot number in the local variable array and must be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:56.014076745Z"}
{"id":"1d966818-d62c-460b-a31e-7597179929b1","expr":"start != end","rationale":"The scope of a local variable is between distinct start and end points. If start equals end, the variable has zero length scope, which is typically invalid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:56.014076745Z"}
{"id":"f4eec224-4492-4b1a-a59f-f54c3d2366ce","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The start label array must be non-null as it represents the start of local variable scope ranges.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.805948295Z"}
{"id":"4cae778a-24cb-4fcf-bb5c-95b206847b55","expr":"end != null","rationale":"The end label array must be non-null as it represents the end of local variable scope ranges.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.805948295Z"}
{"id":"d85cbd33-1a15-40f1-8b68-3ee1bd532d2e","expr":"start.length == end.length","rationale":"The start and end arrays represent corresponding instruction indices for the same local variable ranges, thus must have same length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.805948295Z"}
{"id":"68fd0170-6c3d-4303-957c-f6381bfd62a9","expr":"start.length == index.length","rationale":"The index array holds the local variable's index corresponding to each range in start array, so lengths must match.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.805948295Z"}
{"id":"4be6783c-39de-4dd1-bbc3-08c79e4eb412","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor specifies the class descriptor of the annotation class and must be non-null to identify the annotation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.805948295Z"}
{"id":"52a4a40b-083f-4df4-bfa8-7d11bc0f43ab","expr":"line >= 0","rationale":"Line number parameter is expected to be a non-negative integer representing a source line.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.981737661Z"}
{"id":"0d96bb10-34ac-4396-a06d-f683cb77018a","expr":"start != null","rationale":"According to the method's documentation, the start label must have been visited, indicating it is not null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.981737661Z"}
{"id":"bffa64e4-957c-4bd7-91e6-b1c76eb76728","expr":"start.getOffset() >= 0","rationale":"Since 'start' must have been visited already, its offset should be valid and non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.981737661Z"}
{"id":"dfb0dbd6-a61c-4d0a-a7ba-42763303b3ca","expr":"line <= 65535","rationale":"The caller masks line numbers with 0xFFFF before passing, so line should be within 0 to 65535.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:58.981737661Z"}
{"id":"190a52be-5e3c-4072-8fae-d6323d3ed5d1","expr":"line > 0","rationale":"The 'line' parameter represents a source file line number which is conventionally positive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:59.090379715Z"}
{"id":"88fe1cea-61cb-466f-b300-e45167022ec9","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The 'start' parameter is the first instruction corresponding to this line number and must be non-null to avoid exceptions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:59.090379715Z"}
{"id":"96f2943d-10e5-4ece-8ccf-6735cc99068c","expr":"start.getOffset() >= 0","rationale":"The Javadoc mentions an exception if start is not already visited (visitLabel called), implying start.getOffset() >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:59.090379715Z"}
{"id":"7c7511b7-104b-4c5a-aef3-853407efc688","expr":"! (start.getOffset() < 0)","rationale":"This rewriting emphasizes the requirement that start has been visited.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLineNumber(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:40:59.090379715Z"}
{"id":"bc2b3b8c-47c6-403b-8cc0-7542852d64a1","expr":"result == null || visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"Ensures visible is a boolean and result is either null or non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariableAnnotation(int,TypePath,Label[],Label[],int[],String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:00.354768901Z"}
{"id":"ef7a889f-eba5-4fc6-879a-f538c7d02045","expr":"maxStack >= 0","rationale":"The JVM specifies that maxStack cannot be negative as it represents stack depth","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:00.381189358Z"}
{"id":"1fb66c3b-65b1-4470-b4b4-0cb9d9cdf234","expr":"maxLocals >= 0","rationale":"The number of local variables in a method cannot be negative","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:00.381189358Z"}
{"id":"9a38ceda-fc04-4949-b677-951d81642636","expr":"maxStack <= 65535","rationale":"maxStack must fit in a 16-bit unsigned integer as per JVM specification","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:00.381189358Z"}
{"id":"49d24647-36a2-487a-8fde-38041a735e86","expr":"maxLocals <= 65535","rationale":"maxLocals must fit in a 16-bit unsigned integer as per JVM specification","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:00.381189358Z"}
{"id":"5cccf658-b4e1-4cfe-bff4-fcae6ef15df2","expr":"maxStack >= 0","rationale":"The maxStack parameter represents the maximum stack size used by the method and should never be negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:03.189270782Z"}
{"id":"c447ff52-a4be-4115-9c20-000a9a25dca4","expr":"maxLocals >= 0","rationale":"maxLocals indicates the number of local variables for the method and must be zero or positive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:03.189270782Z"}
{"id":"57a6073a-9dba-4198-a491-d4a3d5a61b13","expr":"maxStack >= maxLocals","rationale":"Typically, the maximum stack size is expected to be at least the number of local variables due to operand stacking, though this might vary.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMaxs(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:03.189270782Z"}
{"id":"03d257ab-64c5-4d03-bb27-5f16736c7764","expr":"result >= 1","rationale":"Handle tags are constant integer tags representing various handle types and typically start from 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getTag():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:05.387647932Z"}
{"id":"25101fc9-daa6-4ac3-a388-45219b4fcb29","expr":"result <= 9","rationale":"The tag is an ordinal value mapped to specific handle types; upper bound is the number of valid types.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getTag():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:05.387647932Z"}
{"id":"b4a970f2-9be2-4be2-99ee-d307380b5e48","expr":"result != 0","rationale":"The tag field never returns zero as it is assigned one of the predefined non-zero constants.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getTag():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:05.387647932Z"}
{"id":"bb57d208-12c8-4036-b854-1a04459781d5","expr":"result > 0 && result <= 9","rationale":"Valid tags lie within a specified range of integer values corresponding to handle kinds.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getTag():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:05.387647932Z"}
{"id":"66bf3be9-65bf-4a95-b374-469266eb151b","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The getOwner() method returns the 'owner' field which is expected to be non-null String.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getOwner():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:06.040883933Z"}
{"id":"7878f63b-3bca-4e15-b36c-3e60de58a4e0","expr":"!result.isEmpty()","rationale":"The owner usually represents a class or internal name, which should be a non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getOwner():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:06.040883933Z"}
{"id":"2776b091-f5bb-4f15-ad2e-8ec0db7e7b22","expr":"result.indexOf('/') == -1","rationale":"Owner string typically represents internal JVM class name without slashes, so '/' is not part of it.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getOwner():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:06.040883933Z"}
{"id":"75a8de2b-bc43-495c-8813-c23a1f89612f","expr":"result.equals(result.trim())","rationale":"The owner string should have no leading or trailing whitespace.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getOwner():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:06.040883933Z"}
{"id":"9c3220e0-7ad3-4bef-bd3c-f987ad2af4ac","expr":"result != null","rationale":"getName() returns the object's name field which is expected to be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getName():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:09.161912156Z"}
{"id":"0320a281-c3bb-4aeb-a49b-d8752bfa0f64","expr":"result.length() > 0","rationale":"The name is likely a valid identifier or descriptor, so it should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getName():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:09.161912156Z"}
{"id":"b6980d7d-7c43-4ea6-ac35-a7afebc19cc9","expr":"result.trim().equals(result)","rationale":"Names generally don't include leading or trailing whitespace.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getName():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:09.161912156Z"}
{"id":"a1d9a0a7-4980-4983-8e4a-3d7546f07132","expr":"object != null","rationale":"The equals method expects a non-null object to proceed with field comparisons.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#equals(Object):boolean","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:11.102156045Z"}
{"id":"380c5f85-46ac-4094-b67c-bd1f01b9ea31","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The descriptor string should always be a valid non-null string representing the handle descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getDesc():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:11.542140055Z"}
{"id":"d5ce1446-d725-4242-8086-d1ee2e01773a","expr":"result.length() > 0","rationale":"A descriptor typically has a positive length representing type descriptors.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getDesc():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:11.542140055Z"}
{"id":"27aa2b03-ebc9-4ab6-840a-0023d7d67407","expr":"!result.contains(\" \")","rationale":"Class file descriptors do not contain spaces.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getDesc():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:11.542140055Z"}
{"id":"06df8ba2-a2a6-4e6f-b9fd-b9bffda2d203","expr":"result.startsWith(\"(\") || !result.contains(\")\")","rationale":"Distinguishing method descriptors from field descriptors by presence of '(' and ')'.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#getDesc():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:11.542140055Z"}
{"id":"7cb68862-7403-4b39-bfdd-5853d0eec16f","expr":"result >= 0","rationale":"The hash code value is masked with 0x7FFFFFFF to ensure a non-negative integer result.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#hashCode():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:13.355503806Z"}
{"id":"8d3141de-1e41-4ec3-99a7-30b0a19213f3","expr":"(result & 0x7FFFFFFF) == result","rationale":"The hash code method applies a mask to clear the sign bit, so result equals result & 0x7FFFFFFF.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#hashCode():int","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:13.355503806Z"}
{"id":"27c87f31-74cf-4310-a18c-e0b876f50004","expr":"flags >= 0","rationale":"Flags are non-negative integer bitmasks in typical usage.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassWriter#hasFlags(int):boolean","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:13.427394074Z"}
{"id":"c5ea6e6f-f17b-414c-9cc4-fff1abdcae46","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The toString method usually returns a non-null string representation.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#toString():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.424077342Z"}
{"id":"6b335a4a-cd0f-49ba-a80b-8880888dcdc0","expr":"result.contains(\".\")","rationale":"The returned string includes the owner and name separated by a dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#toString():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.424077342Z"}
{"id":"1f29d95f-8a90-4b23-8474-d146f826cdb1","expr":"result.endsWith(\")\")","rationale":"The string representation ends with a closing parenthesis.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#toString():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.424077342Z"}
{"id":"6ac3ba63-af96-493c-a94d-aaed070c3318","expr":"result.length() > 5","rationale":"The returned string has a length longer than trivial strings.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Handle#toString():String","file":"org/springframework/asm/Handle.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.424077342Z"}
{"id":"dcef795e-5206-4d06-93da-d882e3e4988b","expr":"name != null","rationale":"At method entry, the 'name' parameter, being the class internal name, is expected to be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassWriter#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.667381131Z"}
{"id":"a0784ad7-1f4b-4dc9-85f5-f475b83a080b","expr":"version >= 0","rationale":"Version is an int representing class version; negative value generally invalid.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassWriter#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.667381131Z"}
{"id":"b3b567e1-4222-4921-b6f4-b370399ecd84","expr":"interfaces == null || (interfaces.length >= 0)","rationale":"The interfaces array can be null or a zero-or-more length array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassWriter#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.667381131Z"}
{"id":"655250a4-3cf3-4706-9760-b502af7da445","expr":"signature == null || signature.length() >= 0","rationale":"Signature can be null or a string with length >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.ClassWriter#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/ClassWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T16:41:17.667381131Z"}
